    {
      "id": "f07cfb42-463e-4d11-8052-afba1cf97d8c",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        256,
        3760
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 700,
        "height": 764,
        "content": "## AI Support Ticket Triage with Observability\n\nAutomatically triages incoming support tickets using Claude Sonnet. High-confidence responses are sent instantly; low-confidence tickets escalate to a human on Slack. Every step is logged to Infini Analytics, correlated by a single execution_id.\n\n### How it works\n1. Webhook receives the ticket and generates a unique execution_id\n2. Claude Sonnet drafts a reply and scores its own confidence\n3. High-confidence replies are sent automatically\n4. Low-confidence tickets are posted to Slack for human review\n5. The final outcome (success or error) is logged to close the run\n\n### Setup\n- [ ] Add your Anthropic API credential\n- [ ] Add your Infini Analytics credential (Bearer Token) and paste your Automation ID into all 5 Infini Analytics nodes\n- [ ] Add your Slack credential and choose a channel/user for escalations\n- [ ] Send a POST request to the Webhook with a `message` field to test\n\n### Customization\n- Adjust the confidence threshold in \"If (high confidence?)\"\n- Swap Slack for email or Microsoft Teams\n- Swap Claude Sonnet for any other supported chat model"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "258a6870-c42b-4935-bc95-4be62d2db1a1",
      "name": "Sticky Note13",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        256,
        4624
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 360,
        "content": "### 1. Receive ticket & log start\nGenerates a unique execution_id and logs the START event in Infini Analytics.\n\n\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "976dc0e1-7a41-4094-a3d3-a5bda64b9669",
      "name": "Sticky Note14",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        928,
        4624
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 680,
        "content": "### 2. AI Agent triages the ticket\nClaude Sonnet reads the ticket, logs its data-table lookup as an EVENT, and drafts a structured reply with a confidence score."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b2e04efc-b637-47e3-97f5-b9a099320981",
      "name": "Sticky Note15",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1360,
        4624
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 892,
        "height": 632,
        "content": "### 3. Route by confidence\nHigh-confidence replies are sent and logged as an EVENT. Low-confidence tickets escalate to Slack and are logged as a WARNING."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c14d7e5c-bbd4-4652-ba54-9c7c76e73795",
      "name": "Sticky Note16",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2304,
        4624
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 632,
        "content": "### 4. Final outcome logging\nLogs the final END event on success, or an ERROR event if any step failed — all under the same execution_id."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
